    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on speed and favorable matchups, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98), who ranks as our premier start. Batting leadoff against Phillips, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an aggressive dynamic platoon edge (+14%) and the premium value we assign to his base-stealing upside. **Christian Yelich** (75.84) also presents an elite profile against Singer, buoyed by a significant +13% platoon adjustment. While **Yordan Alvarez** (68.04) faces a tough left-handed matchup against Rodriguez, his elite xwOBA (0.450) and second-spot order positioning keep his efficiency safely in the \"Strong\" tier. We also anticipate high value from **Caleb Durbin** (65.89), whose aggressive sprint speed profile is maximized by a favorable park factor (+16%), keeping him essential despite facing a difficult arm in Bradish.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Colt Keith** (45.59), who remained our closest consideration for the lineup. While **Colt Keith** showed reasonable potential, the 2.89 xERA of Williams created a difficult hurdle for his offensive ceiling compared to the primary utility options. Ultimately, the optimizer favored the platoon advantages of **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (55.66) and the volume projections for **Josh Smith** (60.34). We continue to monitor the status of **Gary Sanchez**, who remains benched due to a lack of confirmed lineup presence, and we are exercising caution with **Carson Benge** (36.45) and **Dillon Dingler** (33.13), both of whom fell below our 40-point efficiency floor. With **Trea Turner** (65.60) anchoring the middle infield against Mahle, our focus remains on leveraging these high-contact, high-speed spots to maintain our lead in the categories that define the Zurich Zebras' identity.",
